fb: present a frame one swap behind, so it is never still being drawn (0283)

The moving black block is a frame the panel read while CoreAnimation had drawn
only part of it: the region still to come is cleared opaque black, which is why
the block moves with the content. A GPU fence cannot catch it, because the draw
had not been submitted yet when the fence was sampled (0281 measured
scanout_us_max 624us, so that fence always passed instantly).

Present the previous frame instead of the newest: when a newer swap arrives the
pending frame is promoted to a show slot, so it has had a whole swap to finish
before the panel reads it. swapFired() waits for that promotion, and a two-frame
bound flushes a frame that goes stale so boot's first frame and the final frame
before the UI idles still reach the panel.

Off by default (sweetfb_latepresent=1 enables it), so the existing path is
unchanged without the flag. The show slot owns its surfaces exactly like
fPendHold: promotion moves pointers without touching the hold count, replacing a
slot releases the one it replaced, and a failed present is re-queued into the
slot it came from. The GPU gate still runs before the pending frame is taken.

